Before — one method mixes validation, discount calculation, and persistence:

```java
void processOrder(Order o) {
    if (o.getItems().isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("empty order");
    if (o.getCustomer() == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("no customer");
    double total = 0;
    for (Item i : o.getItems()) total += i.getPrice() * i.getQty();
    if (o.getCustomer().getTier() == Tier.GOLD) total *= 0.9;
    if (o.getCustomer().getTier() == Tier.PLATINUM) total *= 0.85;
    db.save(o.withTotal(total));
}
```

Step 1 — Extract Method for validation and pricing:

```java
void processOrder(Order o) {
    validate(o);
    double total = calculateTotal(o);
    db.save(o.withTotal(total));
}

void validate(Order o) {
    if (o.getItems().isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("empty order");
    if (o.getCustomer() == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("no customer");
}

double calculateTotal(Order o) {
    double total = o.getItems().stream().mapToDouble(i -> i.getPrice() * i.getQty()).sum();
    return applyTierDiscount(total, o.getCustomer().getTier());
}
```

Step 2 — Replace Conditional with Polymorphism for the tier discount, so a new tier never needs a new `if`:

```java
double applyTierDiscount(double total, Tier tier) {
    return tier.discountRate() * total; // each Tier enum constant owns its own rate
}
```

Each method is independently readable and independently testable — `validate`, `calculateTotal`, and the persistence call — where the original required tracing one 12-line method to find any one of them.
